2. **Delegate**: Call the Layer 2 Orchestrator
3. **Record**: Unpack the returned `LibraryMeasurements` and add to workspace

**Generic Pattern - Frontend Integration**:
```python
def run(self, workspace):
    """Execute the module (called by CellProfiler pipeline)."""
    # Import the library function for THIS module
    from cellprofiler_library.modules._measurexyz import measure_xyz
    
    # ============================================================
    # STEP 1: Extract inputs from workspace
    # ============================================================
    image = workspace.image_set.get_image(self.image_name.value)
    param1 = self.param1_setting.value  # Module-specific settings
    param2 = self.param2_setting.value
    
    # ============================================================
    # STEP 2: Call library function
    # ============================================================
    if self.wants_objects():
        # Object-level processing path
        object_name = self.object_name.value
        objects = workspace.object_set.get_objects(object_name)
        
        lib_measurements = measure_xyz(
            image=image.pixel_data,
            image_name=self.image_name.value,
            param1=param1,
            param2=param2,
            object_name=object_name,
            labels=objects.segmented
        )
        
    else:
        # Image-level processing path
        lib_measurements = measure_xyz(
            image=image.pixel_data,
            image_name=self.image_name.value,
            param1=param1,
            param2=param2,
            object_name=None,
            labels=None
        )
    
    # ============================================================
    # STEP 3: Unpack LibraryMeasurements into workspace
    # ============================================================
    
    # Add image measurements
    for feature_name, value in lib_measurements.image.items():
        workspace.measurements.add_image_measurement(feature_name, value)
    
    # Add object measurements (if any)
    for obj_name, features in lib_measurements.objects.items():
        for feature_name, values in features.items():
            workspace.measurements.add_measurement(obj_name, feature_name, values)
    
    # Add experiment measurements (if any)
    for feature_name, value in lib_measurements.experiment.items():
        workspace.measurements.add_experiment_measurement(feature_name, value)
```

